## 1. Introduction
Metal–organic frameworks (MOFs) are a fascinating material class that are both fundamentally important and technologically relevant. They have been extensively studied for their rich structural chemistry1–5 and potential applications in numerous areas,6,7 including but not limited to, gas storage,8–10 gas separation,11–15 heterogeneous catalysis,16–20 chemical sensing,21–25
